<title>USA: Bank of Boston sets $200 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Bank of Boston sets $200 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue was priced on Thursday, according to lead manager Morgan Stanley &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>BORROWER BANK OF BOSTON CORP</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	     COUPON 7.375 PCT   MATURITY 09/15/06</p>
<p>TYPE SUB NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.980   PAY DATE 03/15/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY A3	    SPREAD 65 BP	 PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB-PLUS	YIELD 7.378 PCT    FEES STD $6.50</p>
<p>UNDERLYING: 10-YEAR U.S. TREASURY NOTE</p>
